-- title:
--   Hopf quotient by a Hopf subalgebra's augmentation ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and $H$ a commutative ring carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $k$, and let $K'$ be a $k$-subalgebra of $H$ such that (i) for every $x \in K'$ the comultiplication $\Delta(x)$ lies in the $k$-span of the tensors $a \otimes_k b$ with $a, b \in K'$, and (ii) the antipode maps $K'$ into $K'$. The assertion is that there exist a type $Hb$ (in the same universe as $H$) with a commutative ring structure and a Hopf algebra structure over $k$, together with a $k$-bialgebra homomorphism $\pi : H \to Hb$, such that: $\pi$ is surjective; the kernel of $\pi$ as a ring homomorphism is the ideal of $H$ generated by $\{x \in K' : \varepsilon(x) = 0\}$, where $\varepsilon$ is the counit; $\varepsilon(\pi(x)) = \varepsilon(x)$ for all $x \in H$; $\pi$ commutes with the antipodes of $H$ and $Hb$; and for every $k$-subalgebra $K \subseteq H$ satisfying the same two stability conditions (i) and (ii) imposed on $K'$, the image subalgebra $K.\mathrm{map}\,\pi \subseteq Hb$ again satisfies them: the comultiplication of each of its elements lies in the $k$-span of the tensors $a \otimes_k b$ with $a, b$ in that image, and the image is stable under the antipode of $Hb$.
--
--   This is the standard construction of the quotient Hopf algebra $H/K'^{+}H$ attached to a Hopf subalgebra $K'$ of a commutative Hopf algebra, in the dual guise of the quotient of an affine group scheme by a normal subgroup scheme, packaged together with the statement that $\pi$ carries Hopf subalgebras to Hopf subalgebras. It is obtained from the general existence statement for quotients by Hopf ideals, [`HopfAlgebra.exists_hopfAlgebra_bialgHom_surjective_ker_eq_of_hopfIdeal`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_hopfAlgebra_bialgHom_surjective_ker_eq_of_hopfIdeal), and feeds the faithful flatness of a commutative Hopf algebra over a Hopf subalgebra in the reduced case over a perfect field.
